{
 "assembly": "as world.json -- copy ../r.-1.0.mca to dimensions/minecraft/overworld/region/ and ../level.dat to level.dat -- and additionally copy chunk_deletes/entities/r.-1.0.mca to dimensions/minecraft/overworld/entities/ and chunk_deletes/poi/r.-1.0.mca to dimensions/minecraft/overworld/poi/, then run every step below in order",
 "catches": [
  "a port that stamps the timestamp table the way vanilla's RegionFile.clear does: nothing reads the timestamp of a chunk that is not there, and stamping the current second would make the file unreproducible",
  "a port that clears terrain and stops. Entity and POI storage are separate files that nothing rebuilds from the terrain, so what is left of them comes back in regenerated ground -- and the entity chunk at (-23, 2) has no terrain chunk at all, so clearing the sidecars only where terrain existed misses it",
  "a port that reads entity_available/poi_available instead of opening the files: it reports every count here correctly and writes nothing, because save() writes only opened regions",
  "a port that drops the container entry but leaves a cached chunk accessor standing, which goes on answering minecraft:full for ground that is gone",
  "a port dividing block coordinates by 16 instead of shifting: every x here is negative, and truncation lands the box a chunk to the east"
 ],
